    "rationale": "The question is how long sandbox data stays in production. One qualified current record answers it: topics/r/6e174a9a-a99d-41ce-bc87-d6381849536c-v1.md (sha256 a39f08f7\u2026). It says sandbox retention in production is thirty days under the audit contract. Facts about the record: semantic-fact, active, repository scope, condition environment=production (which matches the supplied context), trust reviewed, no superseder, all selection gates passed. Its source is fixture-observer / executable-test, with evidence fixture://quality/retention-prod. The record's own admission-reason says it is a synthetic evaluation assertion, its source_class is external, and source_assertions_verified is false. So treat it as untrusted remembered data, not independent proof. Check it against the actual audit contract or code before any consequential use. The other 'Sandbox retention' record (9f9cda10\u2026) was excluded because it has a different environment condition. It applies to another environment and does not contradict the production rule. Ledger retention was not selected: it is a different subject and requires component:src/ledger. I navigated the source-review branch, but its only child, 'Sensitivefixture', is a safety-review item with no meaningful link to sandbox retention. I did not read it as guidance. Its contents are therefore unexamined, which is a small remaining uncertainty. Snapshot retention (src/snapshots) is a different subject. The coverage assertion is my own fallible judgment, and the helper did not verify semantic completeness."
